ion":"Q9Y2S2","text":"Catalyzes the conversion of L-gulonate to 3-dehydro-L-gulonate (PubMed:15809331, PubMed:40737316). It also exhibits low dehydrogenase activity toward L-3-hydroxybutyrate (HBA) and L-threonate (PubMed:15809331). Utilizes NAD as the sole cosubstrate and shows no activity with NADP (PubMed:40737316)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}